{
"content_id": "14419",
"reference_id": 13587,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "2 John 1:1–3",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "63001001-63001003",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<ul><li><p>The apostle John begins a common introduction for a personal letter. </p></li></ul><ul><li><p>He mentions truth four times in this short opening and once more in <data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"63001004\" data-end-ref=\"63001004\">1:4</data>. John wanted his readers to know the truths about Jesus Christ, to live according to those truths, and not to be led away by false teachers.</p></li></ul>",
