{
"content_id": "14426",
"reference_id": 13594,
"version": "1.0.4",
"title": "2 John 1:4–11",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "63001004-63001011",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "Professional",
"content": "<p>John now applies the truth and love that he mentioned in the introduction (<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"63001001\" data-end-ref=\"63001003\">1:1–3</data>) to the situation of those he is writing to. Living in truth and love means maintaining unity or fellowship with true Christians (<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"63001004\" data-end-ref=\"63001006\">1:4–6</data>). It also involves recognizing false teachers and choosing not to listen to or support them (<data class=\"bible-ref\" data-start-ref=\"63001007\" data-end-ref=\"63001011\">1:7–11</data>).</p>",
"associations": {
